# Engine wave 2. Double.MIN_NORMAL was negative and far too large: it printed -4.49423283715579E307 where the
# pinned JDK prints 2.2250738585072014E-308, and Double.doubleToLongBits(Double.MIN_NORMAL) gave -13510798882111488
# where the JDK gives 4503599627370496 (runtime/test/cases.mjs, D11-double-min-normal). Reported upstream as
# teavm#1316, with the two Float constants teavm-0010 already fixes.
#   - The rule, from the Javadoc and the pinned JDK run black box: MIN_NORMAL is the smallest positive normal double,
#     0x1.0p-1022, so it is above 0, half of it is smaller still (a subnormal), and Math.getExponent gives -1022.
#   - TeaVM's TDouble declared it as -0x1.0P+1022, the sign and the exponent's sign both wrong. Nothing else in
#     TeaVM's classlib or core reads the constant (git grep at the pinned tag), and javac copies a constant's value
#     into the code that reads it, so the fix reaches a box through the compile classlib and the run classlib alike.
#   - Now it is 0x1.0p-1022.
#
# Written from TeaVM's own source (classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/java/lang/TDouble.java), the Javadoc and
# the pinned JDK's observed output; no OpenJDK source was opened (clean room, D14). Written by the controlling
# session (Claude Opus 5.5), a language model whose training may include OpenJDK: the patch adds no name and changes
# one constant in TeaVM's own code, to the value the Javadoc states and the probes show.
#
# Applies to: github.com/konsoletyper/teavm tag 0.13.1 (b3a245b7). teavm-0007, teavm-0009 and teavm-0010 also touch
# TDouble.java, in other lines; this applies with or without them.

diff --git a/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/java/lang/TDouble.java b/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/java/lang/TDouble.java
index e0b05e3..dcb575b 100644
--- a/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/java/lang/TDouble.java
+++ b/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/java/lang/TDouble.java
@@ -29,7 +29,9 @@ public class TDouble extends TNumber implements TComparable<TDouble> {
     public static final double NEGATIVE_INFINITY = -POSITIVE_INFINITY;
     public static final double NaN = 0 / 0.0;
     public static final double MAX_VALUE = 0x1.FFFFFFFFFFFFFP+1023;
-    public static final double MIN_NORMAL = -0x1.0P+1022;
+    // teavm-fork: this was negative and far too large. The Javadoc: MIN_NORMAL is the smallest positive normal
+    // double, 0x1.0p-1022.
+    public static final double MIN_NORMAL = 0x1.0p-1022;
     public static final double MIN_VALUE = 0x0.0000000000001P-1022;
     public static final int MAX_EXPONENT = 1023;
     public static final int MIN_EXPONENT = -1022;
